{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And the Egyptians</b> — two times at the beginning of a parashah: ומצרים מקברים (and the Egyptians bury) [and] ומצרים ילד את לודים (and the Egyptians bore Ludim) — to say that even those who had already died, most of them were dug up." "<b>Burying</b> — ומצרים מקכרים מקברים (and the Egyptians — burying) — burying those who pass through, in the parashah of Gog. And that is what is written: כאשר שמע למצרים יחילו (as when one hears of Egypt, they tremble) — כשמע צוד (like the hearing of Tzor)."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {0 "The text is partially corrupt. The reading '??' could not be resolved. The two cited phrases appear to be the two occurrences of 'ומצרים' at parashah beginnings (here in v. 4 and in Genesis 10:13), read via notarikon as מקברים, 'burying.' The word נחטטו (were dug up) likely refers to the plague striking even the dead.", 1 "The forms מקכרים and מקברים appear to be variant notarikon expansions of the same letters. The verse fragments appear to quote Ezekiel 32:10 (כאשר שמע … יחילו) with the phrase למצרים possibly reflecting a textual variant or misquotation of the Ezekiel passage; כשמע צוד is unclear."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:23:42.882655070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}